  "caption_en": "Same photograph, different detector response. Two fixed FFHQ bona-fide photographs (00042 and 00056), selected before their VIS1 scores, are shown in their existing native-aligned and landmark_complete-history variants. No second contributor was added. The history combines INTER_AREA downsampling before separate alignment/cropping: source00042 changes1024→265px before alignment to512px; source00056 changes1024→249px before alignment to512px. Consequently this is neither a JPEG-only nor a blur-only intervention, and displayed crops are not identical. Every fixed model is retained: released SelfMAD and A/B seed403 last checkpoints. Table scores are uncalibrated sigmoid outputs; delta is history-minus-native in each model's own logit units. No operational threshold, decision flip, error-rate or cross-model robustness ranking is claimed. SelfMAD was chosen as the demonstration model after an earlier private pilot; these two photographs and A/B controls were fixed before the new scores. Cases are potentially exposed development illustrations with unknown person/component/full-training overlap. Private noncommercial research preview only; publication/likeness clearance remains unresolved. No source images were generated, retouched or replaced. No heatmap is shown and no new inference was run for rendering. Source photographs: Rebecca Brown, “Shirtless, bearded Josh.” (FFHQ00042), https://www.flickr.com/photos/rebeccacbrown13/2168341402/ ; RAFFI YOUREDJIAN, “MANGAGAN-7” (FFHQ00056), https://www.flickr.com/photos/62487011@N08/28696918755/ . Both CC BY-NC2.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/2.0/ . FFHQ/FFHQ-Morphs dataset documentation is BY-NC-SA4.0; technical source attribution and transformation descriptions remain in the manifest.",
